@startuml training-hybrid-assembly
' `train hybrid` is an ASSEMBLY step, not a training step: it loads two already-
' trained model files, maps the single CLI --alpha onto whichever strategy was
' selected, and writes the combined model. Dynamic is the only strategy whose
' three struct fields are DERIVED from --alpha rather than set directly, and
' NgramWithEmbeddingFallback ignores --alpha entirely. Those derivations are the
' point of the diagram.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/training-hybrid-assembly.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/training/hybrid.md §4.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #263238
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title train hybrid — assembling two pre-trained experts

rectangle "**NGRAM_MODEL**\nNgramModel::load_portable" as ngram #1565C0
rectangle "**EMBEDDING_MODEL**\nSubwordEmbedding::load" as embed #2E7D32

rectangle "**""--strategy""**\nlinear · log-linear\nngram-fallback · dynamic" as strat #6A1B9A
rectangle "**""--alpha""** (default 0.8)\n**""--cache-size""** (default 50 000)" as knobs #546E7A

rectangle "**Linear**\nalpha = α" as s_lin #6A1B9A
rectangle "**LogLinear**\nalpha = α" as s_log #6A1B9A
rectangle "**NgramWithEmbeddingFallback**\nα is **ignored**" as s_fb #6A1B9A
rectangle "**Dynamic**\nbase_alpha = 0.5·α\nalpha_per_context = 0.1\nmax_alpha = min(α, 0.95)" as s_dyn #6A1B9A

rectangle "**HybridConfig**\nstrategy · cache_size\nembedding_smoothing = 10⁻⁸\ntemperature = 1.0" as cfg #1B6CA8
rectangle "**HybridLanguageModel::new**" as build #1B6CA8
rectangle "**hybrid.bin**\nsave_portable" as out #455A64

ngram --> build : expert 1
embed --> build : expert 2
knobs --> strat
strat --> s_lin
strat --> s_log
strat --> s_fb
strat --> s_dyn
s_lin --> cfg
s_log --> cfg
s_fb --> cfg
s_dyn --> cfg
cfg --> build
build --> out

note bottom of build
  **No corpus is read.** Both experts must already exist
  on disk; changing either one means re-running
  ""train ngram"" / ""train embedding"" and re-assembling.
end note

note right of cfg
  ""embedding_smoothing"" and ""temperature"" are **not**
  CLI flags — they take their ""HybridConfig::default""
  values. Tune them through the library API.
end note

@enduml
